.TH SIMPLE_SHELL 1 "February 2026" "Holberton School" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
simple_shell \- a simple UNIX command interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hsh
.SH DESCRIPTION
simple_shell is a simple UNIX command interpreter. It reads commands from
standard input and executes them in interactive or non-interactive mode.
.SH USAGE
Interactive mode:
.PP
.nf
./hsh
($) ls
($) /bin/ls
($) exit
.fi
.PP
Non-interactive mode:
.PP
.nf
echo "/bin/ls" | ./hsh
cat file_with_commands | ./hsh
.fi
.SH BUILTINS
.TP
.B exit
Exit the shell.
.TP
.B env
Print the current environment.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The shell uses the PATH environment variable to locate executable programs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sh (1),
.BR execve (2),
.BR fork (2),
.BR wait (2)
.SH AUTHORS
See AUTHORS file in the project repository.
